  "AI content payment is not merely a copyright or transaction-efficiency problem; it is a question of political-economic legitimacy. As AI valuations reach hundreds of billions, society asks why the gains from public web content and human knowledge accrue to a few firms. The paper proposes a six-layer tiered data market — from free public content through scarce verified datasets to public benefit-sharing — and defines the AI network democratic economy: rights, pricing, participation, auditability, and returns, each democratized through machine-readable protocols like AICR/AICL.": "Peman pou konteni AI pa zis enn problem drwa-oter ouswa efikasite transaksion; li enn kestion lezitimite politik-ekonomik. Kouma valorizasion AI pe ariv santenn milyar, sosyete pe demande kifer bann gayn ki sorti dan konteni web piblik ek konesans imin al zis dan lame detrwa lantropriz. Sa papye-la propoze enn marse done an sis-kouch, an nivo — depi konteni piblik gratis, atraver bann dataset verifye ki rar, ziska partaz benefis piblik — e li defini lekonomi rezo demokratik AI: drwa, pri, partisipasion, kapasite pou verifye, ek retour, sakenn demokratize atraver bann protokol lizib-pou-masinn kouma AICR/AICL.",
  "AI crawler simulator: four personas (search indexer, RAG assistant, model-training pipeline, commercial redistributor) evaluated against a site’s declarations; undeclared rights surface as uncertainty, illustrating the Protocolized Openness thesis.": "Simulater crawler AI: kat personaz (endekser moter-rode, asistan RAG, pipeline antrennman modèl, redistributer komersyal) ki evalye kont bann deklarasion enn sit; drwa non-deklare paret kouma lensertitid, ki ilistre tez Ouvertir Protokolize-la.",
